    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1413eb5e95587120a367a86aaa148bfd3edd1258818a023c774496c6aa433c61",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The long-polynomial framework turns uniform shifted-divisor correlations into a length-dependent moment weight, so the known k=2 fourth moment can calibrate the proposed correlation error range. Extending the package past eta=1 gives w_2(eta)>2 and conflicts with Ingham's theorem; conditional on retaining the approximate-functional-equation split and length relation, the source therefore locates the failure in accumulated shifted-divisor errors and infers an omitted main-term contribution.",
