    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4d919198dd5340be043bd9ce46aa4d6918b0733802e389920f7a6beea1a71ef2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The approximate functional equation represents one zeta moment by two Dirichlet-polynomial mean squares whose lengths are complementary at conductor scale, while the long-polynomial conjecture assigns each length an explicit weight. Composing those representations makes split-independence a necessary coherence test, and for the sixth moment the identity w_3(eta)+w_3(1-eta)=42 passes it for every permissible split.",
