    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ae0e614fdd52168fa04ff3cc58c1da17461e02aa3048306d1bc5722727079605",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The moment model separates a proved arithmetic suppression, log a_k=-k^2 log(2e^gamma log k)+o(k^2), from a conjectural random-matrix growth law for the normalized factor g_k. In the moment-to-maximum inequality these two large-k contributions combine with the gamma normalization, and optimizing the moment order changes the predicted maximal-order regime according to the assumed growth class of g_k.",
